{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small manufacturing business in Kenya and I need to understand what compliance obligations I might have under the Standards Levy Order. Can you create a simple checklist of the key things I should verify with the relevant authority to make sure I'm meeting current requirements?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's what you need to check on regarding Standards Levy obligations for your manufacturing business:\n\n**Standards Levy Compliance Checklist**\n\n1. **Verify your current levy status** – Confirm whether your business is currently registered under the Standards Levy Order and what your annual obligations are.\n\n2. **Review levy calculations** – Check how your levy amount is determined and ensure the calculation method being applied to your business is correct.\n\n3. **Confirm payment schedules** – Establish the exact payment dates and amounts due for the current year.\n\n4. **Document levy records** – Keep receipts and payment confirmations for all Standards Levy payments made.\n\n5. **Check for exemptions or rate adjustments** – Determine if your business size, sector, or turnover qualifies you for any reduced rates or exemptions.\n\n6. **Understand reporting requirements** – Find out if you need to submit any additional documentation or returns related to the levy.\n\nThe current Standards Levy framework has been in place for some time, so it's worth confirming directly with the Standards body that you're applying the correct rate and meeting all current expectations for your business size and type."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "kebs_standards_levy_msmes_2023.pdf", "source_text": "of a variety of regulatory and non-regulatory policy 26 REGULATORY IMPACT ASSESSMENT FOR THE STANDARDS LEVY ORD