{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm running a small retail shop in Nairobi as a sole proprietor right now, but I'm thinking about bringing in my two brothers as co-owners. Do we need to incorporate as a company, or can we just continue as we are? What does the law say about who can form a company if we decide to go that route?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You have a choice. As a sole proprietor, you can keep operating informally, but if you want to make your brothers formal co-owners with legal protection and clear ownership stakes, incorporation is the cleaner path. Under the Companies Act, 2015, you and your brothers can form a company together by subscribing your names to a memorandum of association. Since you're all individuals, you qualify—the law allows one or more legal persons, which includes individuals like yourselves, to incorporate. This gives you legal structure, limits personal liability, and makes ownership and profit-sharing clear. The exact company type depends on your needs (there are five types available), but for a retail operation with multiple owners, a private company limited by shares is typically the most practical choice. You'll need to register at the Companies Registry once you decide to move forward."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "doing_business_kenya_launch.txt", "source_text": "been incorporated and registered at the Companies Registry under the Companies Act, 2015. Who can incorporate a company? One or more legal persons (which includes individuals, companies, government-owned entities, non-profit organizations and other legal persons excluding an unincorporated Trust) can form a company by subscribing their names to a memorandum of association. Which types of companies are available? There are five types of companies: Company Type Details Private company limited by s"}}
