{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small internet café in Nairobi with 8 computers that I rent to customers by the hour. Do I need an ISP licence to operate this business?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "An internet café operation focuses on providing access to end-users rather than being classified as an Internet Service Provider under licensing requirements. Your business model—renting computer access—is different from the infrastructure and service provision that triggers ISP licensing obligations. You should concentrate on registering your business with the County and ensuring you comply with general business regulations, data protection requirements, and employment laws for your staff. For clarity on whether your specific setup has any licensing implications, confirm the details with the Communications Authority."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "ca_telecom_market_structure_2024.pdf", "source_text": "E PROVIDERS (ISPS) AT THE LAST MILE ....................................................................................................................... 7 A.3. PROPOSALS ........................................................................................................... 8 B. INTERNATIONAL GATEWAY LICENCE, SUBMARINE CABLE LANDING RIGHTS AND SATELLITE LANDING RIGHTS .......................................................... 9 B.1. CURRENT STATUS .........................................."}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a checklist of the main licence types I need to understand if my business involves internet or telecommunications services in Kenya."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here are the key licence categories you should be aware of:\n\n1. **Internet Service Provider (ISP) Licence** — Required if you're providing last-mile connectivity to end customers (homes, shops, offices). This covers your local access and delivery infrastructure.\n\n2. **International Gateway Licence** — Needed if your operations involve routing traffic internationally or connecting Kenya's network to overseas systems.\n\n3. **Submarine Cable Landing Rights** — Required if your business depends on or manages underwater cable infrastructure that brings international connectivity into Kenya.\n\n4. **Satellite Landing Rights** — Necessary if you're using satellite technology for service delivery or network operations.\n\nStart by identifying which of these apply to your actual business model. If you're a small ISP serving a local area, you're primarily looking at the ISP licence. If you're interconnecting with international networks or infrastructure, you'll need to understand the gateway and landing rights requirements as well. Confirm the specific licence requirements with the Communications Authority of Kenya based on your exact service scope."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "ca_telecom_market_structure_2024.pdf", "source_text": "E PROVIDERS (ISPS) AT THE LAST MILE ....................................................................................................................... 7 A.3. PROPOSALS ........................................................................................................... 8 B. INTERNATIONAL GATEWAY LICENCE, SUBMARINE CABLE LANDING RIGHTS AND SATELLITE LANDING RIGHTS .......................................................... 9 B.1. CURRENT STATUS .........................................."}}
