{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small community radio station in Nairobi with about 5 staff members. We've been operating informally for two years and now want to get properly licensed. What do we need to know about the application process for a broadcasting license?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To apply for a broadcasting license, you'll need to watch for an official announcement from the Communications Authority listing the available frequencies or channels that are open for applications. These announcements are published in at least one Kenyan print newspaper and also posted on the CA website—that publication is your signal to start the application process. Once you see the notice, you'll have a specific deadline to submit your application for the license. Make sure you check both print media and the CA website regularly so you don't miss the application window, as the timeframe will be clearly stated in that announcement."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "ca_licensing_procedures.txt", "source_text": "list of available frequencies / channels in at least one print media in Kenya and on the CA website informing interested applicants to apply for provision of the identified broadcasting service (s). Such publication shall be the trigger point for interested applicants to submit application for specific licenses within the time frame specified. Download: Framework on the Application and Usage of DVB Identifiers in Kenya Download: Minimum Technical Requirements for DVB-T2 Receivers in Kenya Proced"}}
