{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm setting up a data centre in Nairobi and I want to know what licences I need to apply for. Can you give me a step-by-step checklist of the licensing requirements I should follow?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's what you need to do:\n\n1. **Identify what services you're providing** — Determine whether your data centre will include any of these: building infrastructure, power supply, servers, internal communication systems, or other related services.\n\n2. **Check if you're building communication infrastructure** — If you're establishing terrestrial and/or non-terrestrial connectivity infrastructure to your facility to help users connect to your data centre, you'll need an NFP-T3 Licence. Apply for this first.\n\n3. **Apply for your ASP Licence** — Since you're operating a data centre that provides building, power, servers, internal communication infrastructure, and related services (but not communication infrastructure in public space), you're required to obtain an Application Service Provider (ASP) Licence.\n\n4. **Prepare your applications** — Gather the documentation needed for both the NFP-T3 and ASP licence applications and submit them to the relevant regulatory authority.\n\n5. **Keep your licences current** — Once granted, maintain compliance with the conditions of both licences.\n\nThe key point: if you're providing the physical facility, power, servers, and internal connectivity to your customers, both licences are mandatory. Confirm the specific application procedures and current requirements with the communications regulator."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "ca_telecom_market_structure_2024.pdf", "source_text": "erator establishes communication infrastructure – terrestrial and/or non-terrestrial connectivity - to the 17 facility to facilitate ease of connectivity by users of this data centre, then they will be required to obtain an NFP-T3 Licence. Requirement for ASP Licence: 77. Data centre operators providing either or all of building, power, servers and internal communication infrastructure and any other related services but excluding communication infrastructure in public space, will be required to"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm setting up a small data centre in Nairobi to lease server space and power to local businesses. I'll provide the building, backup generators, and servers, plus internal network cabling within the facility. I'm not putting in any public telecommunications infrastructure. What licences do I need to get?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You'll need an ASP (Application Service Provider) Licence. Since you're providing the building, power supply, servers, and the internal communication infrastructure within your data centre facility itself, you fall under the ASP licensing requirement. The NFP-T3 Licence would only apply if you were also establishing your own external communication infrastructure—like terrestrial or non-terrestrial connectivity networks—to bring connectivity into the facility from outside. Since you're just setting up the internal systems and leasing space, the ASP Licence is what you need. Confirm the exact application process and current requirements with the Communications Authority."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "ca_telecom_market_structure_2024.pdf", "source_text": "erator establishes communication infrastructure – terrestrial and/or non-terrestrial connectivity - to the 17 facility to facilitate ease of connectivity by users of this data centre, then they will be required to obtain an NFP-T3 Licence. Requirement for ASP Licence: 77. Data centre operators providing either or all of building, power, servers and internal communication infrastructure and any other related services but excluding communication infrastructure in public space, will be required to"}}
