{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "What changes did Kenya make to withholding tax rules starting in October 2019?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "From October 1st, 2019, Kenya expanded which services are subject to withholding tax. Previously, withholding tax mainly applied to management and professional fees. The government broadened this to include additional services beyond those categories. This expansion was designed to widen the tax base and bring more income under withholding tax obligations. If your business pays for services, you should check whether withholding tax now applies to them under these expanded rules."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "doing_business_kenya_sme_guide_2024.pdf", "source_text": "ated by the restructuring of corporate entities in order to allow efficiency and market penetration in corporate entities. Effective Date 1st October 2019 WITHHOLDING TAX Expansion of Withholding Tax Base In order to widen the tax base, The Cabinet Secretary for the National Treasury through Finance Bill 2019 proposed to expand the scope of application of withholding tax by subjecting additional services, other than management and professional fees to withholding taxes. These services include: s"}}
