{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small transport business with 3 matatus that operate in Nairobi. I need a checklist of the annual parking and vehicle-related fees I should budget for. What are my obligations?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's what you need to budget for your 3 matatus:\n\n**Annual Parking Fees Per Vehicle:**\n- Matatu parking fee: KES 2,100 per vehicle per year\n- For 3 matatus: KES 6,300 total\n\n**Loading/Offloading Zone Slots:**\n- If you operate a designated loading or offloading zone, budget KES 114,000 per slot per year\n\n**Clamping Penalties (if applicable):**\n- If any vehicle gets clamped for non-payment, the penalty is KES 2,000 per matatu for each month of default\n- This applies only if you fall behind on payments\n\n**Action steps:**\n1. Confirm with your county or local authority whether all 3 matatus require individual parking permits\n2. Determine if you operate your own loading zone or use a shared one\n3. Set aside the annual parking fees in your business budget before year-end\n4. Keep payment receipts to avoid clamping penalties\n\nVerify the current applicable rates with your county transportation or revenue office, as these may be updated annually."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "mombasa_county_finance_act_2024.pdf", "source_text": "rs and pick ups 1,000.00 90 Mini-bus, Matatus and Canters 2,100.00 91 Buses and Lorries 4,100.00 92 Trailers 6,000.00 93 Loading/Offloading zones for psv per slot per annum 114,000.00 CLAMPING PENALTIES (for clamped vehicles which default on payment for every month defaulted) 94 Saloon cars and Pickups 1,000.00 95 Mini-buses, Matatus and Canters 2,000.00 96 Buses and Lorries 3,000.00 97 Trailers 4,000.00 8. RESERVED PARKING BAYS (per annum per bay) 98 Motors vehicles saloons and pickups, 250,000"}}
