{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I want to start a motor vehicle mechanics business in Kisii. Can you give me a step-by-step checklist of what I need to do to get properly trained and qualified before I launch?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's your path to becoming a qualified motor vehicle mechanic in Kisii:\n\n1. **Enroll in a recognized Level 3 Motor Vehicle Mechanics programme** — Kisii National Polytechnic offers this qualification, which is the standard credential for the trade.\n\n2. **Complete the full Level 3 curriculum** — This covers the technical skills and knowledge you'll need to operate professionally and safely.\n\n3. **Obtain your Level 3 certificate** — Once you pass, you'll have the formal qualification that establishes your credibility with customers and regulators.\n\n4. **Set up your workshop** — With your certificate in hand, you can then establish your business location, tools, and client base.\n\nStarting with formal training at Kisii National Polytechnic gives you both the practical skills and the recognized credential that will make your business legitimate and competitive. Confirm the current programme schedules and fees directly with the polytechnic."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "tveta_tvet_courses_list.txt", "source_text": "The Kisii National Polytechnic View Institutions 265 Motor Vehicle Mechanics Level 3 The Kisii National Polytechnic View Institutions 266 Aquaculture Technology Level 3 The Kisumu National Polytechnic View Institutions 267 Fisheries Technology Level 3 The Kisumu National Polytechnic View Institutions 268 Mobile Phone Repair Level 3 The Nyeri National Polytechnic View Institutions 269 Chemical Production Technology Level 3 The Nyeri National Polytechnic View Institutions 270 Carpentry Level 3 Th"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm starting a small vocational training centre for MSMEs in my area. Can you walk me through the key steps and checkpoints I need to have in place for student enrolment, graduation, and handling dropouts?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's what you need to set up for your training centre's core student management processes:\n\n**Enrolment**: Establish a clear enrolment system that records student intake. Document who enters your programme, when they start, and what they're registering for. Keep these records organized and accessible.\n\n**Graduation**: Define what completion looks like. Set out the requirements students must meet to graduate — whether that's course completion, assessments, or practical competency — and have a formal graduation process that marks their achievement.\n\n**Dropouts**: Create a tracking system for students who leave before completing the programme. Record why they dropped out where possible, and keep this data separate from your active roster. This helps you identify patterns and improve retention.\n\n**Staffing**: Ensure you have qualified staff to manage these processes — someone responsible for admissions records, someone to oversee graduation requirements, and someone tracking student progress and attendance.\n\nYour centre should document all three processes clearly so that every staff member follows the same steps. This also makes it easier if you need to report to education authorities or justify your operations. Check with your county education office on any specific reporting requirements they may have for training centres."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "tveta_annual_returns_report_2023.pdf", "source_text": "........................... 37 6.2 ENROLMENT ...............