{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm thinking about enrolling in a vocational training program to learn a trade skill. How do I check if a training center is properly licensed and legitimate before I sign up?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before you enroll, verify that the vocational training center holds a valid TVETA license. Check the center's license number—it should follow the format TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC with a registration code and year. Look for the license expiry date and confirm it hasn't expired; an expired license means the center is no longer authorized to operate training programs. You can request to see the original license certificate from the center's management, or contact TVETA directly to confirm the license status. Make sure the license shows your specific center's name and location. A properly licensed center gives you assurance that your training will be recognized and that the center meets national standards for vocational education."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "tveta_accredited_institutions.txt", "source_text": "c Wajir 2026-04-25 Expired License Details 604 RUKONGO VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTER TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0057/2016 VTC Public Homabay 2021-04-13 Expired License Details 605 MOYALE VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTER TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0057/2018 VTC Public Marsabit 2023-01-11 Expired License Details 606 MUTWAATHI VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTER TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0057/2019 VTC Public Kitui 2024-01-13 Expired License Details 607 ELDAS VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRE TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0057/2021 VTC Public Wajir 2026-04-25 Expir"}}
