{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "What are the main Level 6 qualification areas offered at St. Paul's University, and what should I know about them if I'm considering staff training for my business?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "St. Paul's University offers Level 6 qualifications across several fields relevant to business operations and service delivery. These include Social Work, Counselling, Community Health, Cosmetology, Information Communication Technology, Software Development, and Network System Administration. If you're thinking about upskilling your team, these are the kinds of professional certifications available at that institution—ranging from technical IT roles to service-based sectors like cosmetology and health-focused areas. The level 6 standard means these are advanced, post-secondary qualifications. Check directly with St. Paul's University for current course details, fees, and whether any align with your business needs."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "tveta_tvet_courses_list.txt", "source_text": "Social Work Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1295 Counselling Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1296 Community Health Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1297 Cosmetology Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1298 Information Communication Technology Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1299 Software Development Level 6 St. Paul's University View Institutions 1300 Network System Administration Level 6 St. Paul's University View Insti"}}
