{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm running a small vocational training centre in Nairobi with about 40 trainees. We operate from a rented commercial space and don't have residential facilities. Which of the infrastructure requirements do I need to have in place right now, and which ones can I phase in later?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "You need to have these facilities operational now: a drainage system with proper sanitation, reliable water supply, a health unit on-site or accessible, and ICT infrastructure for training delivery. You should also have outdoor recreation or sports facilities—even a small courtyard space counts. If your trainees are day-students only (non-residential), you don't need trainee accommodation, kitchen and dining facilities, or laundry and storage for overnight use. However, if you plan to add residential capacity later or take in boarding trainees, you'll need to add kitchen, dining, accommodation with laundry and storage facilities to meet the residential TVET requirements. Make sure any facilities you have can handle your current 40-trainee population without overcrowding. Confirm your specific operational model and facility standards with the TVET regulatory authority to ensure your setup aligns with their current approval requirements."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "tveta_accreditation_handbook.pdf", "source_text": "ies; h. Outdoor recreation facilities in form of games or sports facilities; i. Drainage system, proper sanitation and water supply; j. Health unit; k. ICT infrastructure; and l. Spaces of worship. In addition to the facilities provided above, a residential TVET institution shall provide: m. Kitchen and dining facilities; n. Trainee accommodation, including adequate laundry and storage facilities. NOTE: A TVET institution should have facilities that can accommodate the projected trainee populati"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "What are the main facility requirements that a residential TVET institution in Kenya needs to have?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "A residential TVET institution must provide basic facilities including outdoor recreation and sports areas, a proper drainage system with sanitation and water supply, a health unit, ICT infrastructure, and spaces for worship. On top of these, because students live on campus, you also need to set up kitchen and dining facilities, trainee accommodation with laundry and storage areas. The key point is that all your facilities need to be sized to handle the number of trainees you're actually expecting to enrol—don't build for a number you can't support."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "tveta_accreditation_handbook.pdf", "source_text": "ies; h. Outdoor recreation facilities in form of games or sports facilities; i. Drainage system, proper sanitation and water supply; j. Health unit; k. ICT infrastructure; and l. Spaces of worship. In addition to the facilities provided above, a residential TVET institution shall provide: m. Kitchen and dining facilities; n. Trainee accommodation, including adequate laundry and storage facilities. NOTE: A TVET institution should have facilities that can accommodate the projected trainee populati"}}
